# {{.Name}}

This standalone Go module composes the existing public `profilehttp` reference
backend and `SystemClock` behind `knowndevice-process/0.1-alpha.1`. It uses only
public imports. It is a working fixture/reference wrapper, with no independent
CA, transport, application or hardware integration claim.

The explicit local `replace` in `go.mod` selects the local alpha SDK. The
`v0.0.0` requirement is a local placeholder for
`github.com/knowndevice/knowndevice`; no SDK version has been published. The generated name identifies this
wrapper and does not create another role ID or a new trust policy.

## Build and run the public suite

Use Go 1.27.3 and an available local SDK dependency cache, or normal access to
the pinned modules in `go.mod`/`go.sum`.

```sh
./scripts/ci.sh
```

The executable CI example verifies dependencies, builds the process adapter,
runs tests, and runs the public conformance suite for built-in and process
composition. Each case has fresh generated identities, keys and local TLS
fixture listeners. `fixtures/expectations.json` is read by the test and checked
against the public suite's case list and observed reports. These fixture checks
are `in-memory-model` evidence; they are separate from actual service effects,
controller transition labs, independent adapter authors and hardware validation.

For an existing freshly seeded process lab, select this built executable's
digest when constructing its immutable snapshot. Never replace a binary behind
an active bind mount or change an existing lab's artifact selection.

## Manifest and permissions

`adapter-template.json` declares the implemented contracts and the rule for
deriving exact network origins from the selected public snapshot. It is an
unbound template: it contains no invented origins, executable pin, or profile
selection. The bundled strict `adapter.schema.json` validates both the template
and concrete manifest. To emit a concrete manifest, select the canonical public
snapshot and the exact already-built adapter pinned by that snapshot:

```sh
go run ./cmd/manifest --snapshot /absolute/fresh/public-snapshot.json --adapter /absolute/pinned/adapter
```

This command verifies the executable bytes and process-composition pin, then
prints the exact snapshot/profile/composition/schema digests, sorted
capabilities, normalized HTTPS origins, empty filesystem lists, signer brokerage
and fixed protocol limits. It does not contact a service. Initialization
independently negotiates those same contracts before a domain call.

Filesystem lists are empty because initialize supplies public snapshot bytes.
Network origins come only from the selected application, control, issuance and
transport roles. Private keys remain behind temporary signer references; no key
bytes cross stdio. These declarations and the subprocess do not restrict direct
system calls or establish operating-system isolation.

## Retry, status and unknown results

The wrapper performs no automatic mutation retry. A lost or late response,
timeout, cancellation after dispatch, process crash, or invalid response leaves
attempted effects `unknown`. Cancellation cannot undo remote work or remove
durable controller intent. A fresh session must use the original plan,
reservation, CSR, SPKI and scope for the role's actual authenticated status.
Unknown issuance never permits another `/sign`.

The selected reference control service supplies bounded lookup/import and
status. Raw step-ca operation lookup or idempotency is not invented by this
wrapper. An unavailable capability or incomplete proof returns explicit
unsupported, denial or unknown; it cannot establish absence.

Candidate verification cannot grant activation CAS. Activation requires durable
authenticated Application status, its activation revision, and a fresh
independent observation after switching. Effective retirement requires durable
deny, session evidence, authenticated old access denial and a fresh target
observation. CA revoke, local expiry, a TLS alert, or socket closure alone is
insufficient. The shared SDK still checks complete validity/deadline intervals,
exact authenticated peer leaf/SPKI, generation fencing and strict profiles.

## Generation safety

The generator accepts a new single directory name under an existing absolute
symlink-free root. It refuses traversal, invalid names/modules, symlink
components, existing directories and collisions. File writes use rooted
exclusive creation and never overwrite existing files. Content and modes are
deterministic for identical options. An interrupted or failed generation leaves
its partial directory for inspection; select a new directory to retry.
